1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,402
Today is October 15, 2026.

3
00:00:07,402 --> 00:00:12,427
Overnight, Wall Street faced a sharp repricing across major indices.

4
00:00:12,427 --> 00:00:16,128
The Nasdaq tumbled nearly one point nine percent.

5
00:00:16,128 --> 00:00:20,172
The S and P five hundred dropped one point one percent.

6
00:00:20,172 --> 00:00:24,621
The Dow held virtually flat, down less than a tenth of a percent.

7
00:00:24,621 --> 00:00:29,878
A hotter-than-expected September Consumer Price Index sparked this risk-off wave.

8
00:00:29,878 --> 00:00:34,216
Headline inflation hit three point seven percent year over year.

9
00:00:34,216 --> 00:00:38,898
Core consumer prices rose zero point three percent month over month.

10
00:00:38,898 --> 00:00:46,152
Service inflation accelerated alongside crude oil shocks following missile strikes on Saudi Aramco infrastructure.

11
00:00:46,152 --> 00:00:51,998
Traders quickly doubled the odds of an October Federal Reserve rate hike to nearly fifty percent.

12
00:00:51,998 --> 00:00:56,839
Swaps now price in ninety percent probability for a hike by December.

13
00:00:56,839 --> 00:01:02,341
Furthermore, markets are pricing up to three additional hikes through late twenty twenty-seven.

14
00:01:02,341 --> 00:01:06,067
However, long-duration Treasury yields declined.

15
00:01:06,067 --> 00:01:09,939
The thirty-year yield pulled back for a fifth straight session.

16
00:01:09,939 --> 00:01:16,839
Institutional flows rotated into defensive cash cows, including healthcare and consumer staples.

17
00:01:16,839 --> 00:01:21,275
The S and P five hundred sliced through seven thousand eight hundred.

18
00:01:21,275 --> 00:01:25,785
It now tests its fifty-day moving average at seventy-seven hundred.

19
00:01:25,785 --> 00:01:32,586
Crucially, the seven-six-twenty floor represents the line separating consolidation from a true bear reversal.

20
00:01:32,586 --> 00:01:38,591
Meanwhile, tech and artificial intelligence infrastructure bore the brunt of liquidity liquidation.

21
00:01:38,591 --> 00:01:42,917
The Philadelphia Semiconductor Index slid over four percent.

22
00:01:42,917 --> 00:01:46,814
Over one trillion dollars in market value evaporated.

23
00:01:46,814 --> 00:01:50,429
Yet, this drawdown is not a demand crisis.

24
00:01:50,429 --> 00:01:55,613
ASML posted record third-quarter net income of five billion euros.

25
00:01:55,613 --> 00:02:00,405
Customers are already reserving photolithography tools through twenty thirty.

26
00:02:00,405 --> 00:02:02,978
The bottleneck is not appetite.

27
00:02:02,978 --> 00:02:07,145
The bottleneck is the cost of financing capital expenditures.

28
00:02:07,145 --> 00:02:10,650
High interest rates squeeze levered compute plays.

29
00:02:10,650 --> 00:02:15,809
Second-tier cloud infrastructure providers face heavy refinancing hurdles.

30
00:02:15,809 --> 00:02:23,175
Take CoreWeave, ticker C R W V. Shares plunged fifteen point five percent in a high-volume gap down.

31
00:02:23,175 --> 00:02:26,851
The company carries fifty-two billion dollars in debt.

32
00:02:26,851 --> 00:02:30,552
Its unsecured bonds yield over fifteen percent.

33
00:02:30,552 --> 00:02:35,944
A nine percent cost of capital clashes with four to five percent target yields.

34
00:02:35,944 --> 00:02:40,834
Investors must monitor the sixty to sixty-five dollar prior swing low.

35
00:02:40,834 --> 00:02:44,670
Watch for base building before attempting any bottom fishing.

36
00:02:44,670 --> 00:02:51,410
Next, Oracle, ticker O R C L. Oracle slid nine percent, hitting mid-summer lows.

37
00:02:51,410 --> 00:02:54,878
Total debt exceeds one hundred billion dollars.

38
00:02:54,878 --> 00:02:59,829
Credit default swaps widened as leverage pushed toward five hundred percent.

39
00:02:59,829 --> 00:03:05,491
High-yield debt contagion in cloud infrastructure is now the primary systemic vulnerability.

40
00:03:05,491 --> 00:03:13,628
Finally, in semiconductors, ASML, ticker A S M L, and SK Hynix present stark divergences.

41
00:03:13,628 --> 00:03:20,135
ASML fell four percent despite raising full-year sales guidance to forty-five billion euros.

42
00:03:20,135 --> 00:03:24,841
Advanced node capacity constraints remain locked through twenty twenty-eight.

43
00:03:24,841 --> 00:03:29,621
SK Hynix sits down twenty-five percent, deeply oversold.

44
00:03:29,621 --> 00:03:36,165
Delayed orders for sixth-generation high-bandwidth memory packaging triggered heavy foreign selling across Seoul.

45
00:03:36,165 --> 00:03:42,476
However, short-covering relief rallies could emerge as technical support catches oversold momentum.

46
00:03:42,476 --> 00:03:48,125
Capital is separating balance-sheet fortresses like Microsoft from high-yield debt borrowers.

47
00:03:48,125 --> 00:03:52,121
Keep cash reserves intact and respect support zones.

48
00:03:52,121 --> 00:03:56,128
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

49
00:03:56,128 --> 00:04:00,295
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
